# MW (MEMORY CHANNEL WRITE) - Set-direction frames
# Source: Yaesu FTDX10 CAT Operation Reference Manual, revision 2308-F.
#   Position chart: printed page 17 (PDF page 18), block "MW MEMORY CHANNEL WRITE",
#   Set chart (the Read and Answer rows of that chart are printed empty; the
#   Control Command List on printed page 5 likewise gives MW as Set=O, Read=X,
#   Ans.=X, so Set is the only direction that exists for MW).
# Derived 29/07/2026 by hand from the position chart and its parameter legend only.
# NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document was consulted.
#
# Frame length: 28 bytes. Field map read off the chart's numbered positions:
#   1-2    "MW"
#   3-5    P1  memory channel, 3 chars  (legend: 001-099, P1L-P9U (PMS))
#   6-14   P2  frequency in Hz, 9 digits
#   15-19  P3  clarifier direction (1) + clarifier offset (4), 0000-9990 Hz
#   20     P4  0: RX CLAR "OFF"  1: RX CLAR "ON"
#   21     P5  0: TX CLAR "OFF"  1: TX CLAR "ON"
#   22     P6  MODE nibble
#   23     P7  '0' (Fixed)   <- MW legend gives P7 as fixed 0, no Read vocabulary
#   24     P8  0: CTCSS "OFF"  1: CTCSS ENC/DEC  2: CTCSS ENC
#   25-26  P9  "00" (Fixed)
#   27     P10 0: Simplex  1: Plus Shift  2: Minus Shift
#   28     ";" terminator
#
# NOTE - MINUS SIGN: vector 2 uses ASCII HYPHEN-MINUS 0x2D for the P3 minus
#   direction. The 2308-F legend renders that glyph as a double dash ("--: Minus
#   Shift"); the same legend for the IF command on printed page 14 renders it as a
#   single "-". The single ASCII 0x2D byte is an INHERITED ASSUMPTION.
# NOTE - ZERO OFFSET SIGN: '+' is used when the clarifier offset is 0000. The
#   manual defines only two direction characters and does not say which one
#   accompanies a zero offset. INHERITED ASSUMPTION.
#
# Hardware status: UNVERIFIED. Neither frame has been sent to or captured from a
#   real FTDX10.
# Format: name<TAB>frame
mw_ch003_14m250_usb_simplex_noclar	MW003014250000+000000200000;
mw_ch021_29m600_fm_minusshift_rxclar_ctcss	MW021029600000-050010401002;
